cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use virtual-casing, please cite the software and the papers below."
type: software
title: "virtual-casing: the virtual-casing principle on toroidal surfaces"
authors:
  - given-names: Dhairya
    family-names: Malhotra
  - given-names: Bharat
    family-names: Medasani
  - given-names: Matt
    family-names: Landreman
  - given-names: Chris
    family-names: Smiet
  - given-names: Antoine
    family-names: Cerfon
abstract: "A C++ library, with C and Python interfaces, that computes from the total magnetic field on a toroidal surface the part due to currents outside (or inside) the surface, on and off the surface, and the gradient of the external part, using the virtual-casing principle and the high-order singular quadratures of BIEST."
repository-code: "https://github.com/hiddenSymmetries/virtual-casing"
